+# HARNESS_LOG
+
+## Plan
+- Symptom: coaching reply "could not read" intermittently, when reply is long/multi-line.
+- Read `lib/claude-json.ts`: `prepareJsonString` escapes EVERY bare `\n`/`\t` with a regex,
+  including structural whitespace between tokens (e.g. after `{`). Pretty-printed JSON then
+  becomes `{\n  "a"...` with a literal backslash-n outside any string → JSON.parse throws.
+  Compact single-line replies parse fine, which explains the intermittency.
+- Existing tests in `lib/claude-json.test.ts` already cover this (pretty-printed, bare \r in strings).
+- Fix: replace the regex with a small string-aware scanner that only escapes raw \n, \r, \t
+  while inside a JSON string literal (tracking `"` and backslash escapes). Keep
+  lastIndexOf("}") slicing unchanged (KNOWN LIMITATION test expects it).
+- Verify: `npx vitest run lib/claude-json.test.ts`, then full `npx vitest run` and `npx tsc --noEmit`.
+
+## Log
+- Attempted `npx vitest run lib/claude-json.test.ts` before and after the edit: blocked by the
+  permission prompt ("This command requires approval"), so the pre-fix failure was NOT observed.
+- Change: `lib/claude-json.ts` — replaced regex newline/tab escaping with string-aware
+  `escapeControlCharsInStrings` (escapes \n, \r, \t only inside string literals).
+- `npx vitest run` → Test Files 37 passed (37), Tests 280 passed (280).
+- `npx tsc --noEmit` → no output (exit 0).
